#
#   dpkg-buildpackage -Ppkg.bucklespring.nolibinput
#   dpkg-buildpackage -Ppkg.bucklespring.nox11

Package: bucklespring-libinput
Architecture: linux-any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.bucklespring.nolibinput>
Depends: bucklespring-data (>= ${source:Version})
Suggests: bucklespring-data-vain, bucklespring-data-sequential, bucklespring-data-synth,
 gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Provides: bucklespring
Conflicts: bucklespring (<< 1.5.1-2~)
Replaces: bucklespring (<< 1.5.1-2~)
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - libinput flavour
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing.
 .
 It runs as a background process and plays back the sound of each key
 pressed and released on the keyboard, just as if using an IBM
 Model-M. The sound of each key has carefully been sampled, and is
 played back while simulating the proper distance and direction for a
 realistic 3D sound palette of pure nostalgic bliss.
 .
 This flavour reads the key events straight from the raw input devices
 in /dev/input through libinput instead of from X11, so it also works
 under a Wayland compositor and on the console. Those devices are not
 readable for ordinary users out of the box; a debconf question, asked
 at medium priority and answered no by default, offers to grant the
 access to the user at the local seat, see README.Debian. It is
 registered as an alternative for /usr/games/buckle.

Package: bucklespring-x11
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!pkg.bucklespring.nox11>
Depends: bucklespring-data (>= ${source:Version})
Suggests: bucklespring-data-vain, bucklespring-data-sequential, bucklespring-data-synth,
 gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Provides: bucklespring
Conflicts: bucklespring (<< 1.5.1-2~)
Replaces: bucklespring (<< 1.5.1-2~)
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - X11 flavour
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing within an X session.
 .
 It runs as a background process and plays back the sound of each key
 pressed and released on the keyboard, just as if using an IBM
 Model-M. The sound of each key has carefully been sampled, and is
 played back while simulating the proper distance and direction for a
 realistic 3D sound palette of pure nostalgic bliss.
 .
 This flavour grabs the key events through X11, and thus only sounds
 for keys typed within an X session. It is registered as an
 alternative for /usr/games/buckle; see bucklespring-libinput for the
 Wayland and console flavour.

Package: bucklespring
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: bucklespring-libinput | bucklespring-x11
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - transitional package
 This is a transitional package, pulling in bucklespring-x11 or
 bucklespring-libinput now that the program is shipped in one binary
 package per key event source. It can safely be removed.

Package: bucklespring-data
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Breaks: bucklespring (<< 1.5.1-2~)
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - Model M clips
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing.
 .
 It runs as a background process and plays back the sound of each key
 pressed and released on the keyboard, just as if using an IBM
 Model-M. The sound of each key has carefully been sampled, and is
 played back while simulating the proper distance and direction for a
 realistic 3D sound palette of pure nostalgic bliss.
 .
 This package contains the IBM Model M recordings the program began with,
 the clip set named "bucklespring". It is the set used when none is asked
 for, and the one the other sets borrow from for keys they do not cover, so
 every flavour needs it.
 .
 The alternative clip sets are in bucklespring-data-vain,
 bucklespring-data-sequential and bucklespring-data-synth.

Package: bucklespring-data-vain
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - vain's clips
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing.
 .
 This package contains the clip set named "vain-qwertz": a full QWERTZ
 layout recorded by vain, with two to four takes of every key, one of them
 chosen at random for each press.
 .
 Select it with "buckle --clips=vain-qwertz" or from the preferences window.

Package: bucklespring-data-sequential
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - SequentialDesign's clips
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing.
 .
 This package contains the clip set named "sequential": a keyboard recorded
 by SequentialDesign with two to four takes of every key, one of them chosen
 at random for each press.
 .
 Select it with "buckle --clips=sequential" or from the preferences window.

Package: bucklespring-data-synth
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: Nostalgia bucklespring keyboard sound - synthesised clips
 Bucklespring emulates the sound of an old IBM Model-M space saver
 bucklespring keyboard while typing.
 .
 This package contains the clip sets which are generated rather than
 recorded: "piano", a pentatonic scale rising from left to right across the
 keyboard; "drums", a kick, snare, hat or tom per key; "slapstick", boings
 and slide whistles; and "beeper", a single beep for a Model M with its PC
 speaker wired up.
 .
 They are made by tools/make-clips.py in the source, so any of them can be
 remade or altered.
 .
 Select one with "buckle --clips=piano" or from the preferences window.
